{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KioiwwEdQxxgausrU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\n**Bring the Majestic Back**\n\nThe Majestic on Main Street went dark in 2022. Before it closed, it was selling about 180 tickets a week. Since then the nearest cinema has been 38 miles away, so seeing a film means a 76-mile round trip.\n\nWe can change that. The building's owner has agreed to rent the Majestic to us for $1 a year for ten years if we raise $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and fix the roof.\n\nA local bank has pledged $25,000 if we raise the other $60,000 by June 30. Three local businesses have already pledged $11,000 in writing.\n\n**If you gave last time**\n\nThree years ago we tried to raise $120,000. We reached $47,000 and refunded every dollar. This goal is $35,000 lower, and a bank and three businesses have committed before the campaign even opens. The promise is the same as last time: this is all-or-nothing. If we don't reach $85,000 by June 30, every pledge is returned in full.\n\n**If we make it**\n\nForty-six volunteers have already signed up to run the box office and the snack bar. We plan to reopen by Thanksgiving. Every three months we'll post a public report at the town library showing how the money was spent.\n\n**Two things you should know up front**\n\nOur roof estimate is from last fall, and the contractor has told us it could rise by as much as 15%. We also can't promise every new release in its opening week, because that depends on the film distributors.\n\nThe campaign runs from May 1 to June 30. Please pledge what you can, and tell a neighbor. Let's turn the lights back on at the Majestic.\n\nRuth Albers\nChair, [Group name]\n</final_document>\n\nIt's about 290 words. A few things to settle before it goes out:\n\n- **The $11,000 from local businesses.** I didn't say whether it counts toward the $60,000. If it does, consider saying \"only $49,000 to go,\" because that's a stronger line. If it's on top of the $60,000, that should be made clear instead.\n- **The roof could go up by 15%.** The pitch admits this, but it doesn't say who would cover the extra. Readers will ask. If you have an answer (a contingency, the businesses, more fundraising), adding one sentence would close the gap.\n- **Whether the cinema can stay open.** Since you don't have running costs or a break-even figure yet, I left them out rather than guess. It's the most likely question from skeptics, so it's worth preparing an answer for the campaign page FAQ.\n- **Placeholders.** The group name is still a placeholder, and rewards and the platform can be added once you've decided."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":10253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1047},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d19f40c6-de8b-4f2f-8d29-a351301333ef","uuid":"c88d15ec-b500-4870-a64d-d1c6bbe9eef6","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:33:43.608Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KioTKXgkqhV8t38ymb"}
